      "message": "I suggest making hook_call_deferred() into a macro, so that we don\u0027t have to change how it\u0027s invoked everywhere. We currently have this:\n\n  void foo(void) { ... }\n  DECLARE_DEFERRED(foo);\n\n  hook_call_deferred(foo, 0);\n\nThe current CL would change that to\n\n  void foo(void) { ... }\n  DECLARE_DEFERRED(foo);\n\n  hook_call_deferred(\u0026__deferred_foo, 0);\n\nwhich is not at all obvious. \n\nUsing a macro to automatically prepend \"\u0026__deferred_\" to the function name would be much more readable.",
